    <dashboard name='Documentation'>
      <repository-location derived-from='https://tableau.deliveryhero.net/t/GlobalStandardReporting/workbooks/AffordabilityTracker_16632398031120/Documentation?rev=' id='Documentation' path='/t/GlobalStandardReporting/workbooks/AffordabilityTracker_16632398031120' revision='' site='GlobalStandardReporting' />
      <style />
      <size maxheight='900' maxwidth='1000' minheight='900' minwidth='1000' sizing-mode='fixed' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='4' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone forceUpdate='true' h='62913' id='3' type-v2='text' w='98400' x='800' y='36198'>
            <formatted-text>
              <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10' underline='true'>Methodology</run>
              <run fontalignment='1'>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>- The base dataset has the restaurants&apos; ordered items data.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>- Using this dataset, we take the average item price for each calendar month for every restaurant.

- All ordered item prices are compared with the Big-Mac-Price of the country for that month.  </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>All prices are in local currencies</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>, and we use Big Mac price of items in that country to have the same comparison base between contries. 
</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Example</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>: In Turkey Big Mac is 40 Liras, and AFV of Turkey is 60 Liras; in turn the AFV X -average price in terms of big macs is  60/40=1.5X</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>- Only vendors with </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>shop_type = &quot;restaurants&quot;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> are included.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>- Item data for an entity is considered good if:</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>        The share of items </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>priced above zero</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> is </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>more than 80%</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>,</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>        and the share of items </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>priced above 5xBMI</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> is </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>less than 15%</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>,</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>        and the share of items </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>priced above 10xBMI</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> is </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>less than 5%</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>- For entities considered, these items are </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>excluded</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>:</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>        Items </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>priced below 0.5xBMI</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> or </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>below the price at the 20th percentile, whichever is the highest</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>        Items </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>priced above 10xBMI</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontsize='10'>- In addition to the BMI-based item exclusion, the following filtering is used:</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontsize='10'>        For each restaurant, items are ranked by total GMV (their contribution to the restaurants GMV).</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontsize='10'>        Going from top to bottom, only the items with contributions to the &quot;top&quot; 75% of the restaurant&apos;s GMV.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontsize='10'>        As the &quot;top&quot; 75% of the GMV can be provided with a smaller percentage of items, many items from the long tail may get excluded by this rule.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>Affordability Index is calculated as the </run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>mean item price of each restaurant as a multiple of the country&apos;s BMI</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>.</run>
              <run>Æ&#10;</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>On the city/entity levels, Affordability Index is the order-weighted average of the restaurants&apos; indices.</run>
              <run>&#10;&#10;----&#10;</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10' underline='true'>BMI</run>
              <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'>:</run>
              <run fontcolor='#000000' fontsize='10'> Big Mac Index = price of a Big Mac Burger in a country</run>
            </formatted-text>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='4' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone h='35309' id='239' is-scaled='1' param='Image/bigmac indexxss.png' type-v2='bitmap' w='98400' x='800' y='889'>
            <zone-style>
              <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
              <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
              <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
              <format attr='margin' value='4' />
            </zone-style>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <devicelayouts>
        <devicelayout auto-generated='true' name='Phone'>
          <size maxheight='700' minheight='700' sizing-mode='vscroll' />
          <zones>
            <zone h='100000' id='263' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
              <zone h='84000' id='262' param='vert' type-v2='layout-flow' w='84000' x='8000' y='8000'>
                <zone fixed-size='280' h='35309' id='239' is-fixed='true' is-scaled='1' param='Image/bigmac indexxss.png' type-v2='bitmap' w='98400' x='800' y='889'>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
